/target

# Python bytecode from the benchmark tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Typeset preview of the generated artifacts. A build output, not a source:
# the .tex and .tsv it is made from are committed and checked by
# `paper.py --check`, and a binary that changes on every run would churn the
# history without adding anything reviewable. Rebuild with `make paper`.
paper/generated/artifacts.pdf

# Claude Code's local state: a machine-specific permission allowlist and a
# transient session lock. Both are per-checkout, both name local paths and
# hosts, and neither means anything to anyone else's clone.
.claude/
